.TH "SCCFM-CLI OBJECTS NETWORK-GROUP CREATE" "1" "2026-08-19" "0.39.4" "sccfm-cli objects network-group create Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-objects\-network-group\-create \- Create a network group.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli objects network-group create
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a network group.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-name TEXT
The name of the object.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-r,\fP \-\-referenced\-object TEXT
UID or name of an existing network object to include (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-network\-literal\fP TEXT
Inline network literal (IP, CIDR, or range; repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-url\-literal\fP TEXT
Inline URL literal (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-d,\fP \-\-description TEXT
A human-readable description of the object.
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-labels TEXT
Labels to attach to the object (can be specified multiple times).
.TP
\fB\-t,\fP \-\-tags TEXT
Tags in key=value format (value can be comma-separated; repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Run a preflight check without performing the operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
